    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mtext>of source</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><msup><mfenced><mtext>distance</mtext></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br />Here, we assume light to spread uniformly in all directions.<br />The number of photo-electrons emitted from a surface depends on the intensity of light&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math> falling on it. Thus the number of electrons emitted&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> depends directly on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math>.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> remains constant as the source is the same.<br />&nbsp;<br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8756;</mo> </mrow> </math> &nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></math><br />&nbsp;<br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8756;</mo> </mrow> </math> &nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mi>P</mi><mi>P</mi></mfrac></mfenced><msup><mfenced><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mn>1</mn><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mn>4</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></math>"
